<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asyut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asyut is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a>. It was the northern terminus of the Darb al-Arba'in, the 'Forty Days Road' caravan route that linked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. Through it the Darfur Sultanate and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a> exported goods such as enslaved people, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrich-feather">ostrich feathers</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asyut.jpg" alt="Asyut" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roland Unger · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AsyutSalamTaggatLibrary.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
